𝗗𝗮𝘆 15 𝗼𝗳 𝟯𝟲𝟬 days of LeetCode Challenge.

𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗯𝗹𝗲𝗺 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 :-1292. Maximum Side Length of a Square with Sum Less than or Equal to Threshold.
Given a m x n matrix mat and an integer threshold, return the maximum side-length of a square with a sum less than or equal to threshold or return 0 if there is no such square.

𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗯𝗹𝗲𝗺 𝗹𝗶𝗻𝗸:- https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-side-length-of-a-square-with-sum-less-than-or-equal-to-threshold

𝗛𝗶𝗻𝘁:- Hint: Use 2D prefix sums of matrix and then followed by either binary search or greedy approach.

Code:- 


public class Solution {
    public int MaxSideLength(int[][] mat, int threshold) {
        int m = mat.Length;
        int n = mat[0].Length;
        int[,] pref = new int[m + 1, n + 1];

        // 1. Build 2D Prefix Sum table
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                pref[i, j] = mat[i - 1][j - 1] + pref[i - 1, j] + 
                             pref[i, j - 1] - pref[i - 1, j - 1];
            }
        }

        int maxK = 0;
        // 2. Search for the largest k
        for (int i = 0; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++) {
                // While a larger square starting here is within bounds 
                // and satisfies the threshold, increment maxK
                while (i + maxK + 1 <= m && j + maxK + 1 <= n && 
                       GetSum(pref, i, j, maxK + 1) <= threshold) {
                    maxK++;
                }
            }
        }

        return maxK;
    }

    private int GetSum(int[,] pref, int i, int j, int k) {
        // Returns the sum of the k x k square starting at (i, j)
        return pref[i + k, j + k] - pref[i, j + k] - pref[i + k, j] + pref[i, j];
    }
}
